<article class="env-definition" id="0125">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0125">Definition <span data-tag="0125">12.16.1</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an additive category. The <em>category of graded objects of $\mathcal{A}$</em>, denoted $\text{Gr}(\mathcal{A})$, is the category with </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
objects $A = (A^ i)$ are families of objects $A^ i$, $i \in \mathbf{Z}$ of objects of $\mathcal{A}$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
morphisms $f : A = (A^ i) \to B = (B^ i)$ are families of morphisms $f^ i : A^ i \to B^ i$ of $\mathcal{A}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>